@title Lesson walk: cooler-layout (search, headline, moves, apply, undo)
@area Learn
# The step in each picture is in its name: a ticked action step moves the card on by itself, and an action step has no Next button. The lesson from the palette, in the cooler-layout sample. Do it for me only carries out commands, so the Cooler layout button and Apply the moves are really clicked. The search takes about a minute on a worker thread. The window opens in the Cabinet, over the plate; on this sample it finds moves that cool the neighbours while the hottest device stays over its limit, which the lesson says.
key ctrl+k
wait 4
text cooler layout
wait 6
click_text "Cooler places for hot devices: cooler layout"
wait 40
shot 01-why
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 02-open-cabinet
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 03-heat-on
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
shot 04-press
check_layout
click_text "Cooler layout" Button
wait_s 120
expect "Apply the moves"
expect "Model estimate"
shot 05-headline-step-search-done
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 06-moves-step
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 07-limits-step
check_layout
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 08-apply-step
check_layout
click_text "Apply the moves" Button
wait 20
expect "Moved"
shot 09-applied-undo-step
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 20
shot 10-undone
check_layout
